From 3cf6a6884781d9f0d9aa89766dab9b0a4bb5c8de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrey Borodin <amborodin@acm.org>
Date: Sat, 30 May 2026 23:07:39 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add isolation test: SSI serialization failure swallowed
 by SAVEPOINT

A serialization failure raised by predicate.c while a transaction is
identified as the pivot of a dangerous structure ("Canceled on conflict
out to pivot ..., during read", and likewise "during write") aborts the
current transaction via ereport() WITHOUT first marking the transaction
SXACT_FLAG_DOOMED.

If that error is raised inside a subtransaction, ROLLBACK TO SAVEPOINT
swallows it and the transaction is free to COMMIT, defeating
serializable isolation.

This test sets up a two-transaction write-skew.  s2 performs its write
before the savepoint, then reads inside the savepoint and is correctly
cancelled by SSI; it rolls back to the savepoint and commits.  On an
unpatched server the COMMIT succeeds, leaving both writes committed (a
non-serializable outcome).  The expected output reflects the correct
behavior, where the COMMIT fails with a serialization error, so this
test fails until the accompanying predicate.c fix is applied.

Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>
